CV PLACEHOLDER
==============

This file exists only so the "Download CV" button in index.html does not point at a
missing file.

To finish the setup:

1. Export your own CV as a PDF (one or two pages, A4, filename without spaces).
2. Name it exactly:  [YOUR-CV].pdf   (or pick your own name).
3. Save it into this assets/ folder, replacing this placeholder file.

   NOTE: browsers refuse to open a real .pdf containing plain text, so delete this
   placeholder once the real file is in place.

4. Update the download link in index.html, section #home:

       <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="assets/[YOUR-CV].pdf" download>

   Replace "[YOUR-CV].pdf" with your actual filename, for example:

       <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="assets/jahidul-islam-cv.pdf" download>

   Use the SAME name in capitalisation — file names are case-sensitive on
   GitHub Pages, Netlify, and Vercel servers even though Windows is not.

5. Optional: add `target="_blank" rel="noopener"` if you would rather the PDF open
   in a new tab than download.